{%- comment -%}
  SHUDHI — Story split (image / text band)

  A full-bleed photo on one side, an editorial column on the other. The Our Story
  page instantiates this TWICE ("Our Beginning" left-media on cream, "Why We
  Started" right-media on the warmer beige), so every difference between the two
  is a setting: media_position, bg and the copy. Nothing about either instance is
  hardcoded here.

  Deliberately NOT wrapped in .sh-wrap. A max-width wrapper would stop the photo
  short of the viewport edge; instead the copy box re-creates the wrap's gutter
  itself, exactly as .sh-story does (shudhi-home.css:704-714). See the CSS block
  for the arithmetic that keeps it aligned with every other section past --sh-max.

  DOM order is media-then-copy in BOTH positions; the swap is done in CSS via
  grid-column, driven by data-media-position on the root. That is what lets the
  <=767px stack put the photo first without a second markup path — and it keeps
  the reading order photo-then-prose for screen readers in both variants.

  The headline is split into a plain part and an emphasised tail rather than
  accepting HTML, the same bargain sh-story-hero.liquid:11 makes: the gold words
  stay merchant-editable in the theme editor without opening a rich-text hole.
  Unlike the hero, <em> here keeps its italics — the approved design sets
  "today." / "self-care." in gold italic.

  The id is a SETTING, never a literal: this section renders more than once per
  page and a hardcoded id would be duplicated. It has to be author-set rather
  than derived, because Shopify's own wrapper id for a JSON-template section is
  `shopify-section-template--<theme_id>__<key>` — the theme id changes on every
  duplicate/publish, so nothing in the theme can link to it reliably.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- assign s = section.settings -%}

<section class="sh sh-split"
         {%- if s.anchor_id != blank %} id="{{ s.anchor_id | handle }}"{% endif %}
         data-media-position="{{ s.media_position }}"
         style="--sh-split-bg:{{ s.bg }};--sh-split-h:{{ s.min_height }}px;">

  <div class="sh-split__grid">

    <div class="sh-split__media">
      {%- if s.image != blank -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          Height is derived from the asset's real aspect_ratio rather than
          hardcoded: the attributes exist to declare the intrinsic ratio, and a
          guessed one would describe an image the merchant never uploaded.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- assign img_h = 1400 | divided_by: s.image.aspect_ratio | round -%}
        <img class="sh-split__photo"
             src="{{ s.image | image_url: width: 1400 }}"
             {%- comment -%} No fallback to the eyebrow. image.alt is nil until a
                 merchant fills it in, and "Our Beginning" describes the band,
                 not the photograph — it would be an inaccurate alternative
                 (WCAG 1.1.1) that also repeats the eyebrow two elements later.
                 Empty alt matches the placeholder branch below, which treats
                 the same slot as decorative. {%- endcomment -%}
             alt="{{ s.image.alt | escape }}"
             width="1400" height="{{ img_h }}"
             loading="lazy" decoding="async">
      {%- else -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          Final photography is not in yet. An empty <img> would render as a
          broken-image glyph and read as a bug in review; this block is tinted
          from the band's own surface colour so the composition, the feathered
          seam and the copy alignment can all be judged on a page that still
          looks finished. Silent by design — aria-hidden, no placeholder text.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <div class="sh-split__photo sh-split__photo--blank" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    <div class="sh-split__copy"{% if s.animate %} data-reveal{% endif %}>

      {%- if s.eyebrow != blank -%}
        <div class="sh-split__eyebrow sh-eyebrow">{{ s.eyebrow }}</div>
      {%- endif -%}

      <h2 class="sh-split__title sh-serif">
        {{ s.heading }}{% if s.heading_em != blank %} <em>{{ s.heading_em }}</em>{% endif %}
      </h2>

      {%- if s.body != blank -%}
        <p class="sh-split__text">{{ s.body }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- comment -%} Both halves required, the same rule sh-story-hero.liquid:69
          applies to its secondary CTA. A label with no destination used to fall
          back to href="#", and an empty fragment means "top of the document" —
          so a reader who reached this band and pressed the link was thrown back
          to the hero, losing their place with no announcement (WCAG 2.4.4).
          Hiding the link is the honest failure mode; a dead one is not. {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if s.link_label != blank and s.link_url != blank -%}
        <a class="sh-split__link sh-btn sh-btn--ghost" href="{{ s.link_url }}">
          {{ s.link_label }} {% render 'sh-icon', name: 'arrow-right' %}
        </a>
      {%- endif -%}

    </div>

  </div>
</section>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "SH · Story Split",
  "class": "index-section",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "text", "id": "eyebrow", "label": "Eyebrow", "default": "Our Beginning" },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Headline" },
    { "type": "paragraph", "content": "The heading is split in two: the plain part, then the tail shown in gold italic." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading", "default": "From tradition to" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "heading_em", "label": "Heading — gold italic tail", "default": "today." },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Copy" },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "body", "label": "Body text", "default": "Our journey began with time-honored herbal rituals passed down through four generations. Inspired by ancient wisdom and family practices, we create products that bring balance and well-being to modern lives." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "link_label", "label": "Link label",
      "info": "Set this and the URL below together — neither renders on its own." },
    { "type": "url", "id": "link_url", "label": "Link URL",
      "info": "The link stays hidden until this is set — a labelled link with no destination jumps the reader back to the top of the page." },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Media" },
    { "type": "image_picker", "id": "image", "label": "Image",
      "info": "Full-bleed to the viewport edge on its side. A neutral tinted panel stands in until one is picked." },
    { "type": "select", "id": "media_position", "label": "Image side", "default": "left",
      "info": "Below 768px the image is always shown first, whichever side is chosen.",
      "options": [ { "value": "left", "label": "Left" }, { "value": "right", "label": "Right" } ] },
    { "type": "range", "id": "min_height", "label": "Band height", "min": 380, "max": 760, "step": 20, "default": 520, "unit": "px" },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Appearance" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "anchor_id", "label": "Anchor id",
      "info": "Optional. Lets another section link straight to this band with #your-id. Must be unique on the page." },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "animate", "label": "Animate on scroll", "default": true },
    { "type": "color", "id": "bg", "label": "Background", "default": "#f6ede1",
      "info": "The panel colour, and the colour the photo's inner edge feathers into. Keep it light — the heading, body and link colours are tuned for a light surface." }
  ],
  "presets": [ { "name": "SH · Story Split" } ]
}
{% endschema %}
